    "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses #12562 (partial — step 1/2 for the \"remove draft_probs\" TODO).\n\nThe `tree_speculative_sampling_target_only` kernel treats `draft_probs` as a scratch output buffer that gets fully overwritten with rejected-token probabilities during verification. The callers were initialising it with `torch.zeros_like(target_probs)` every time, which is wasted work: `(bs, num_draft_tokens, vocab_size)` can be large and the kernel never reads the initial zeros.\n\nThis PR:\n\n1. Replaces `torch.zeros_like` with `torch.empty_like` in both call sites (`dflash_utils.py`, `eagle_utils.py`) for the tree-verification path.\n2. Adds clarifying doc-comments on the `draft_probs` parameter in both the JIT wrapper (`kernels/ops/speculative/sampling.py`) and the AOT wrapper (`kernels/aot/python/sgl_kernel/speculative.py`) so future contributors don't repeat the mistake.\n3. Leaves a TODO pointing at the next step — removing `draft_probs` from the kernel interface entirely, which will require matching C++/CUDA changes.\n\n### Testing\n\n- `torch.empty_like` has identical shape/dtype/device semantics to `zeros_like`, so kernel input validation (which only checks shape/dtype/device) is unaffected.\n- Behavioural change: none. The kernel writes every slot before reading, so the uninitialised memory in `empty_like` is safe.\n- Not run locally (no GPU in this environment). CI will cover kernel correctness.\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] DCO / CLA signed (commit has `Signed-off-by: yancy`)\n- [ ] Tests pass\n- [ ] CI green\n\n---\n\n@lm-sys @LMSYS-org Could one of you please take a look? Happy to iterate on the comment wording. Follow-up PR will tackle the CUDA-side cleanup once this lands.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38468166142](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38468166142)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38468166137](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38468166137)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38468166172](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38468166172)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
